draft: true
id: E553
title: Separate upstream CTest execution from cross-built target consumer runtime
scope: conan ctest cross compile ohos target validation
symptoms: Cross-built test executable cannot run on the Windows build host, while upstream tests need complete execution
root_cause: Host and target test identities are different execution environments even when they share source and test names
repair: Run the complete upstream CTest inventory in an independent host build, then run a target-linked consumer only on the authorized device
verification: Upstream CTest 1/1 and pugixml target consumer 1/1 with clean exit
boundaries: Host CTest cannot substitute for target runtime; target consumer cannot be counted as upstream test coverage
